            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#NaryaDocs"} Narya docs
          %h4#in_other_dependent_type_theories In other dependent type theories
          %p There are other dependent type theories in which it is possible to define indexed semi-simplicial types in a universe:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A first sketch of a definition was given in by
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#Voevodsky12"} Voevodsky (2012)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"} Vladimir Voevodsky
                proposed
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+System"} Homotopy Type System
                (HTS), a homotopy type theory extended with non-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+types"} fibrant types
                and with an extra equality which is extensional in the sense of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#PartLuo15"} Part &amp; Luo (2015)
                proposed a “Logic-enriched Homotopy Type Theory”, in particular, they formalized a construction of semi-simplicial types in this logic using the Plastic proof assistant;
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#AltenkirchCapriottiKraus16"} Altenkirch, Capriotti &amp; Kraus (2016)
                proposed a two-level type theory generalizing HTT, leading to 2LTT by
                = succeed "," do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Dannil Annenkov
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Dannil+Annenkov"} ?
                = succeed "," do
